  "notes": [
   "The catalog prints one rule, 'Select a minimum of 15 units from at least four groups below.' (15.00), over seven groups. It is recorded as one choose_units block of 15. The added rule that the units come from at least four groups is not captured by the block structure.",
   "Group membership: Group 1 Arts (ARTH-C1100 through THE-35, incl. FST-3, MUS, THE); Group 2 Natural, Behavioral, and Social Sciences (ANT, BIO-19, CHE-17, ECON-6, GEG, POLS); Group 3 Business Administration (BUS-40, 43, 46, 48); Group 4 World Languages (ARA, CHI, FRE, ITA, JPN, RUS, SPA); Group 5 English, Humanities, and Philosophy (ENGL, ETS-13, HUM, PHI); Group 6 History (HIST); Group 7 RCCD Study Abroad Program.",
   "Group 7 - RCCD Study Abroad Program allows 'Any course taken while participating in an RCCD Study Abroad Program.' It is not recorded as a course entry.",
   "The Group 6 - History heading has a stray '3.00' printed beside it. The rest of the list gives no reason for it, so it is not recorded as a group minimum.",
   "The catalog prints history courses as HIST-2, HIST-16, HIST-17, HIST-18, HIST-19, HIST-35, HIST-42 and HIST-60. The closed list stores these as 'HIS 2', 'HIS 16', etc. with matching titles. They are treated as the same courses (catalog_addition false); a reviewer should confirm the subject-code change.",
   "ARTH-C1100, ARTH-C1100H, ARTH-3 and ARTH-15 are not in the closed list and are marked as catalog additions.",
   "Cross-listed pairs are printed as separate entries and kept separate: ECON-6/POLS-6, ENGL-8/HUM-8 and ETS-13/PHI-14.",
   "Honors twins are recorded as alternatives of their base course.",
   "The description states 15 units, matching 'Total : 15.00'.",
   "The program learning outcomes are printed for this certificate and recorded as printed.",
